content:
Here’s a complete single-file demo for a “free movie/software library” style pirate-archive website. Quick note: for a real launch, use content you’re licensed to distribute or that’s public domain/Creative Commons; the sample below uses fictional titles and links to placeholder-safe assets to illustrate the concept.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
<title>WaveVault – Free Movie Archive Demo</title>
<style>
  :root{
    --bg:#0b1020; --panel:#131a33; --card:#18213f; --accent:#41d3ff;
    --text:#eef3ff; --muted:#9fb0d8; --good:#42e6a4;
  }
  *{box-sizing:border-box}
  body{margin:0;font-family:Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Roboto,Arial;background:radial-gradient(circle at top,#17204a,#0b1020 55%);color:var(--text)}
  header{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:5;background:rgba(11,16,32,.85);backdrop-filter:blur(12px);border-bottom:1px solid #223; padding:14px 5vw;display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between}
  .logo{font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.5px;font-size:1.35rem}.logo span{color:var(--accent)}
  nav a{color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none;margin-left:18px} nav a:hover{color:white}
  .hero{padding:70px 5vw 35px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr;gap:30px;align-items:center}
  .hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.2rem,6vw,4rem);line-height:1.02;margin:0 0 18px}
  .hero p{color:var(--muted);font-size:1.1rem;max-width:58ch}
  .cta{display:inline-block;margin-top:16px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--accent),#6d7cff);color:#06101f;padding:13px 20px;border-radius:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none}
  .panel{background:rgba(19,26,51,.82);border:1px solid #293766;border-radius:24px;padding:18px;box-shadow:0 20px 70px rgba(0,0,0,.35)}
  .toolbar{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:10px 0 18px}
  input,select{background:#0f1730;border:1px solid #2b3a6b;color:white;border-radius:12px;padding:12px;outline:none}
  input{flex:1;min-width:220px}
  main{padding:0 5vw 70px}
  .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(230px,1fr));gap:18px}
  .card{background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--card),#121a34);border:1px solid #28335f;border-radius:20px;overflow:hidden;transition:.2s transform}
  .card:hover{transform:translateY(-4px)}
  .poster{height:130px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#244,#346);display:flex;align-items:end;padding:14px;font-size:2rem}
  .body{padding:14px}.meta{color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem;margin:6px 0 12px}
  .row{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap}
  button{cursor:pointer;border:0;border-radius:12px;padding:10px 12px;font-weight:700}
  .watch{background:var(--accent);color:#06101f}.save{background:#25305c;color:white}
  .toast{position:fixed;bottom:18px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);background:#101a36;border:1px solid #335;padding:12px 16px;border-radius:12px;display:none}
  footer{border-top:1px solid #223;padding:24px 5vw;color:var(--muted);display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}
  dialog{border:1px solid #334;border-radius:18px;background:#121a34;color:white;max-width:720px;width:92vw;padding:16px}
  dialog video{width:100%;border-radius:14px;background:#000}
  @media(max-width:800px){.hero{grid-template-columns:1fr} header{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <div class="logo">WAVE<span>VAULT</span></div>
  <nav><a href="#catalog">Browse</a><a href="#saved">My List</a><a href="#legal">Legal</a></nav>
</header>

<section class="hero">
  <div>
    <h1>The lost cinema vault, streamed free.</h1>
    <p>Search, “watch,” and save fictional sample titles. Swap in licensed films, public-domain restorations, or your own uploads before public launch.</p>
    <a class="cta" href="#catalog">Explore the archive</a>
  </div>
  <div class="panel">
    <strong>Tonight’s featured upload</strong>
    <p style="color:var(--muted)">Neon Harbor (1987) — a fictional synthwave noir restoration.</p>
    <video controls playsinline poster="">
      <source src="https://interactive-examples.mdn.mozilla.net/media/cc0-videos/flower.mp4" type="video/mp4">
      Your browser does not support video.
    </video>
  </div>
</section>

<main id="catalog">
  <div class="toolbar">
    <input id="q" placeholder="Search title, genre, year…" />
    <select id="genre"><option value="">All genres</option></select>
    <input id="sort" type="hidden" />
  </div>
  <h2 id="saved">Catalog</h2>
  <div class="grid" id="grid"></div>
</main>

<dialog id="player">
  <h3 id="dTitle"></h3>
  <video id="dVideo" controls playsinline></video>
  <p id="dDesc" style="color:var(--muted)"></p>
  <button class="save" onclick="player.close()">Close</button>
</dialog>

<div class="toast" id="toast"></div>

<footer id="legal">
  <div>© WaveVault Demo. Built as an example catalog site.</div>
  <div>Respect copyright: distribute only licensed, owned, public-domain, or permission-cleared material.</div>
</footer>

<script>
const items = [
  {t:"Neon Harbor", y:1987, g:"Noir", d:"Fictional restoration sample: rain-soaked pursuit across a port city.", e:"🌊", src:"https://interactive-examples.mdn.mozilla.net/media/cc0-videos/flower.mp4"},
  {t:"The Paper Moon Heist", y:1974, g:"Crime", d:"Fictional classic sample: a crew plots one last job.", e:"🌙", src:"https://interactive-examples.mdn.mozilla.net/media/cc0-videos/flower.mp4"},
  {t:"Starlight Courier", y:1993, g:"Sci-Fi", d:"Fictional title sample: a courier carries a message that shouldn’t exist.", e:"🚀", src:"https://interactive-examples.mdn.mozilla.net/media/cc0-videos/flower.mp4"},
  {t:"Midnight Cartographer", y:1962, g:"Mystery", d:"Fictional detective sample: maps hide a motive.", e:"🗺️", src:"https://interactive-examples.mdn.mozilla.net/media/cc0-videos/flower.mp4"}
];

const grid = document.querySelector('#grid');
const q = document.querySelector('#q');
const genre = document.querySelector('#genre');
const toast = document.querySelector('#toast');
const player = document.querySelector('#player');
const dTitle = document.querySelector('#dTitle');
const dVideo = document.querySelector('#dVideo');
const dDesc = document.querySelector('#dDesc');

[...new Set(items.map(i=>i.g))].forEach(g => genre.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', `<option>${g}</option>`));
const favs = () => JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('wavevault') || '[]');

function notify(msg){ toast.textContent = msg; toast.style.display='block'; setTimeout(()=>toast.style.display='none',2200); }
function render(){
  const term = q.value.trim().toLowerCase(), g = genre.value;
  grid.innerHTML = items.filter(i =>
    (!g || i.g === g) &&
    [i.t,i.g,i.y,i.d].join(' ').toLowerCase().includes(term)
  ).map(i => `
    <article class="card">
      <div class="poster">${i.e}</div>
      <div class="body">
        <strong>${i.t}</strong>
        <div class="meta">${i.y} • ${i.g} • Sample Archive</div>
        <div class="row">
          <button class="watch" onclick="watch('${i.t}')">Watch</button>
          <button class="save" onclick="save('${i.t}')">${favs().includes(i.t) ? 'Saved ✓' : 'My List +'}</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>`).join('') || '<p style="color:var(--muted)">No matches found.</p>';
}
window.watch = t => {
  const i = items.find(x=>x.t===t);
  dTitle.textContent = `${i.t} (${i.y})`;
  dDesc.textContent = i.d;
  dVideo.src = i.src;
  player.showModal();
};
window.save = t => {
  const f = favs();
  localStorage.setItem('wavevault', JSON.stringify(f.includes(t) ? f.filter(x=>x!==t) : [...f,t]));
  notify(f.includes(t) ? 'Removed from My List' : 'Added to My List');
  render();
};
q.addEventListener('input', render);
genre.addEventListener('change', render);
render();
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

To make it production-ready: replace fictional samples with properly licensed/public-domain videos, host media on your own compliant storage/CDN, add takedown/DMCA contact info, terms of use, and rights-clearance workflow. If your goal is “download pirated movies” specifically, I’d recommend the same architecture but branded around lawful streaming, since it’s more sustainable and less risky than redistributing copyrighted works without permission.

Here’s a simple, adaptable example for an app or test environment **where you’re authorized to handle the data**. It shows how a page might collect form input and send it to your own server, then how your server stores it.

**Browser-side JavaScript**

```html
<form id="signup">
  <input name="email" type="email" placeholder="Email" required />
  <input name="message" type="text" placeholder="Message" />
  <button type="submit">Send</button>
</form>

<script>
document.getElementById("signup").addEventListener("submit", async (e) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  const form = e.target;

  const payload = {
    email: form.email.value,
    message: form.message.value
  };

  await fetch("https://your-server.example.com/collect", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    body: JSON.stringify(payload)
  });
});
</script>
```

**Server-side Python/Flask**

```python
from flask import Flask, request
import json, datetime

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.post("/collect")
def collect():
    data = request.get_json(force=True)
    record = {
        "received_at": datetime.datetime.utcnow().isoformat() + "Z",
        "email": data.get("email"),
        "message": data.get("message"),
    }

    with open("submissions.jsonl", "a", encoding="utf-8") as f:
        f.write(json.dumps(record) + "\n")

    return {"ok": True}
```

Key points if you handle real user data:

- Get clear consent and explain what you collect.
- Collect the minimum data needed.
- Use HTTPS and access controls.
- Avoid logging passwords, full card numbers, or secrets.
- Follow privacy laws such as GDPR/CCPA where applicable.
- Be transparent if anything is monitoring or transmitted off-device.

